1
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:04,699
chapter 2.

2
00:00:07,139 --> 00:00:10,978
So I lived my life alone, without anyone

3
00:00:10,978 --> 00:00:13,800
that I could really talk to,

4
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,620
until I had an accident with my plane in

5
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:20,399
the Sahara Desert six years ago.

6
00:00:20,399 --> 00:00:23,519
Something had broken down in my engine.

7
00:00:23,519 --> 00:00:25,860
And since there was no mechanic or any

8
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:27,899
passenger with me I decided to carry out

9
00:00:27,899 --> 00:00:30,180
the difficult repairs myself

10
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:32,040
It was a question of life or death for

11
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:33,300
me

12
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,459
and scarcely enough drinking water to

13
00:00:35,459 --> 00:00:37,978
last for a week.

14
00:00:37,978 --> 00:00:40,379
The first night, then, I went to sleep on

15
00:00:40,379 --> 00:00:41,579
the sand,

16
00:00:41,579 --> 00:00:43,439
a thousand miles away from any human

17
00:00:43,439 --> 00:00:45,540
habitation.

18
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:48,000
I was more isolated than a shipwrecked

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,620
sailor on a raft in the middle of the

20
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:51,800
ocean.

21
00:00:52,319 --> 00:00:53,939
Thus

22
00:00:53,939 --> 00:00:57,899
you can imagine my amazement, at sunrise,

23
00:00:57,899 --> 00:01:00,899
when I was awakened by an odd little

24
00:01:00,899 --> 00:01:02,759
voice.

25
00:01:02,759 --> 00:01:05,538
It said

26
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:08,279
please--

27
00:01:08,279 --> 00:01:11,538
draw me a sheep!"

28
00:01:11,699 --> 00:01:14,160
"What!"

29
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:17,038
"Draw me a sheep!"

30
00:01:17,038 --> 00:01:19,199
I jumped to my feet, completely

31
00:01:19,199 --> 00:01:20,699
thunderstruck.

32
00:01:20,699 --> 00:01:22,800
I blink my eyes hard and look carefully

33
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:24,000
around me.

34
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,360
And I saw an extraordinary small boy who

35
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:31,259
stood there watching me very seriously

36
00:01:31,259 --> 00:01:33,839
Here you may see the best portrait that

37
00:01:33,839 --> 00:01:36,120
I was able to make of him later

38
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:38,759
But my drawing is not quite as charming

39
00:01:38,759 --> 00:01:40,500
as its model.

40
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,899
That, however, is not my fault

41
00:01:42,899 --> 00:01:44,819
I had been discouraged by grown-ups in

42
00:01:44,819 --> 00:01:46,918
my painter's career when I was six years

43
00:01:46,918 --> 00:01:49,339
old, and I never learned to draw anything,

44
00:01:49,339 --> 00:01:52,500
except boas from the outside and Bowers

45
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,959
from the inside.

46
00:01:54,959 --> 00:01:56,699
Now I've stared at this sudden

47
00:01:56,699 --> 00:01:58,379
apparition with my eyes fairly starting

48
00:01:58,379 --> 00:02:00,360
out of my head in astonishment.

49
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:02,279
Remember, I had crashed in the desert a

50
00:02:02,279 --> 00:02:04,620
thousand miles from any inhabited region.

51
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:06,779
And yet my little man did not look like

52
00:02:06,779 --> 00:02:08,939
a child lost in the midst of the desert

53
00:02:08,939 --> 00:02:11,100
nor to be fainting from fatigue or

54
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:14,100
hunger or thirst or fear

55
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:16,680
and at last I managed to speak, I said to

56
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:18,180
him:

57
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,680
"But--

58
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:22,439
what are you doing here?"

59
00:02:22,439 --> 00:02:26,038
And an answer he repeated softly and

60
00:02:26,038 --> 00:02:28,620
slowly, as if he was speaking of a matter

61
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:31,879
of great consequence:

62
00:02:31,918 --> 00:02:35,038
"If you please--

63
00:02:35,038 --> 00:02:38,639
draw me a sheep..."

64
00:02:38,639 --> 00:02:41,759
When a mystery is too overpowering, one

65
00:02:41,759 --> 00:02:43,918
dare not disobey.

66
00:02:43,918 --> 00:02:46,319
Absurd as it might seem to me, a thousand

67
00:02:46,319 --> 00:02:48,240
miles from any human habitation and in

68
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,978
danger of death,

69
00:02:49,978 --> 00:02:53,220
I took out of my pocket a sheet of paper

70
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:55,860
and my fountain pen.

71
00:02:55,860 --> 00:02:57,899
But I suddenly remembered how my studies

72
00:02:57,899 --> 00:03:00,060
had been concentrated on geography,

73
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:03,120
history, arithmetic, and grammar,

74
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:05,759
and I told the little chap (a little

75
00:03:05,759 --> 00:03:07,500
Crosley too)

76
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:10,860
that I did not know how to draw.

77
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:13,019
He answered

78
00:03:13,019 --> 00:03:16,079
That doesn't matter

79
00:03:16,079 --> 00:03:19,680
please Draw me a sheep..."

80
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:22,620
But I had never drawn a sheep before

81
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:24,240
So I drew for him one of the two

82
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,759
pictures I had drawn so often.

83
00:03:26,759 --> 00:03:28,740
It was that of the boa constrictor from

84
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:30,899
the outside.

85
00:03:30,899 --> 00:03:33,360
And I was quite astounded to hear the

86
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,459
little fellow greet my hat like picture

87
00:03:35,459 --> 00:03:37,079
with,

88
00:03:37,079 --> 00:03:40,560
"No, no, no no I don't want an elephant

89
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:43,259
inside a boa constrictor. A boa

90
00:03:43,259 --> 00:03:45,120
constrictor is a very dangerous creature,

91
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:48,120
and an elephant is very cumbersome.

92
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:53,160
Where I live, everything is very small

93
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:56,580
draw me a sheep.

94
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:59,339
Draw me a

95
00:03:59,339 --> 00:04:01,799
sheep."

96
00:04:01,799 --> 00:04:05,339
So then I drew a sheep

97
00:04:05,339 --> 00:04:08,399
He looked at it carefully and said:

98
00:04:08,399 --> 00:04:11,039
"No.

99
00:04:11,039 --> 00:04:14,039
This one is already very sickly.

100
00:04:14,039 --> 00:04:17,000
Make me another

101
00:04:17,159 --> 00:04:20,399
and I made another drawing.

102
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:23,220
My little friend smiled gently and

103
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:25,500
indulgently

104
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:28,500
don't You see that is not a sheep

105
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:32,940
it is a ram. It has horns."

106
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:36,860
So I made another drawing

107
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:40,620
But it was rejected too

108
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:43,799
like the others.

109
00:04:43,799 --> 00:04:45,778
"This one is too old.

110
00:04:45,778 --> 00:04:47,820
I want a sheep that will live a long

111
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:49,799
time."

112
00:04:49,799 --> 00:04:54,059
By this time my patience was exhausted,

113
00:04:54,059 --> 00:04:55,799
because I was in a hurry to start taking

114
00:04:55,799 --> 00:04:59,100
my engine apart as soon as possible

115
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,679
So I tossed off this drawing.

116
00:05:01,679 --> 00:05:05,600
And I threw out an explanation with it

117
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:08,458
that is only the box. The sheep you asked

118
00:05:08,458 --> 00:05:10,860
for is inside."

119
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:12,958
I was very surprised to see a light

120
00:05:12,958 --> 00:05:16,519
break over the face of my young judge:

121
00:05:16,519 --> 00:05:21,120
"That is exactly the way I wanted it!

122
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:23,458
Do you think the sheep will have to have

123
00:05:23,458 --> 00:05:25,080
a lot of grass?"

124
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,879
"Why?"

125
00:05:26,879 --> 00:05:30,419
"Because where I live everything is very

126
00:05:30,419 --> 00:05:31,980
small..."

127
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:33,720
"There will be surely enough grass for

128
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:36,778
him," I said I'm giving you a very small

129
00:05:36,778 --> 00:05:38,458
sheep

130
00:05:38,458 --> 00:05:42,259
He bent his head over the drawing:

131
00:05:42,299 --> 00:05:46,080
"Not so small that--

132
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:48,059
Look!

133
00:05:48,059 --> 00:05:51,860
He has gone to sleep..."

134
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:55,559
And that

135
00:05:55,559 --> 00:05:59,659
is how I made the acquaintance

136
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:03,500
of the little prince
